-- title:
--   Invariant function with poles over the other supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ a positive integer with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $\ell_g$ a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`).
--
--   **Data downstairs.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); $\kappa_A$ denotes its residue field. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` over $\kappa_A$ which by `hW` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and such that $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q κ_A` (those $j$ for which every elliptic curve of that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point). By `hle` the base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the full level-$M'$ modular function field to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction of constants, a scaling property, and a degree- and order-preserving map on places. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally $s \in W$ is a distinguished supersingular place.
--
--   **Data upstairs.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$ (`hπ`); write $A_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` assert that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Auxiliary-level data consist of a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`) and $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖtA`, `hϖt`), together with $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ equal to $\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`) and a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$ (`hAb`), with $\varpi_b \ne 0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); and $\xi \in k_0$, a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`). The level group is $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, which by `hH₁` is the intersection of `levelH q M'` (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The hypothesis `htame` states that $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$.
--
--   The field $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ equal to `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)` (`hKℓ`), carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$; $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is non-zero and equal to the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb k₀ jq` of the $q$-expansion of $j$ (`hjℓ`). The chart algebra is `chartAlgFin A₀ K_ℓ jℓ`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and $y$ is a maximal ideal of it (`hy`) containing the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`). Further data: $\tilde B = B_t$, an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$; $W_t$, a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $B_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n$, $m$; $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and $\tau_0 \in \mathrm{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$; $\zeta_c$ in the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$; $a_0 \in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. Here `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` expresses that $\tau$ realises on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral expansions the slash action of the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, after any embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$.
--
--   **Hypotheses on $y$.** `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`. `hover`: $y$ lies over $s$, in the sense that for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and such that `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, one has $g - c \in y$ for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$. `hOrbit`: every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra which contains $\pi_0$ and lies over $s$ in exactly this sense is a translate of $y$: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and, for $f$ in it, $f \in y$ if and only if $\tau f \in y'$.
--
--   **The rigid-chart hypotheses.** The hypothesis `hS1` (a conjunction of thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ and $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, is the localisation of $B_t$ at the complement of its maximal ideal, and contracts on the chart algebra to $y$; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa_0$ of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho : B_t \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ₀`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel consists of the elements of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is compatible with reduction of constants and equivariant for level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$ there is $c \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathtt{hAction}(\dots) \circ \rho$, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$, and with the pair $(1,c)$ realised by some further $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau'$; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is hit by a level automorphism from the centre of $W_t$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   Further: $1 \le n$ and $n \mid q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`); $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ and preserves $W_t$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`); $1 \le m$ and $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'$ times a unit of $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`); $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`); `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, and differs from $a_0$ by an element of $y$ (`hjK`, `hjC`, `ha₀y`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hR7` (a conjunction of eleven clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ does not for $0 < k < n$, and every level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ members, is permuted by the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, transitively so, and each member is preserved by $\tau_0$, distinct members being separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$, stable under level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every member of `ends`, each member being the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements that are units there; a level automorphism mapping a member of `ends` into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each member $O$ of `ends` is contained in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, and every element of $O$ differs from a constant by a non-unit, and carries a local crossing model: elements $c_x, c_y \in O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$ for a unit $u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` over $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$ (the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by $XY - \pi_0^m$) carrying constants to constants, $c_x$ and $c_y$ to unit multiples of the two crossing parameters $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ mapped to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, and with $\tau_0$ transported to an automorphism $\theta_0$ acting on $U$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c$ and its inverse modulo the square of the maximal ideal; and, for each such $O$, a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ and an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x$ with the expected properties (a discrete valuation ring $W_x$ containing $O$ and the chart algebra, meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, uniformised by $\pi_0$, with residually transcendental elements including `jqNModC k₀ q`, separating $c_x$ from $c_y$, contracting into $y$ without being centred at $y$, and detecting $O$ among the members of `ends`; a finite-type $B_x \subseteq B_t \cap O$ stable under level automorphisms, with poles only where $j_\ell$ has poles, presenting $O$ as a localisation, and containing an element lying in no valuation subring of the relevant type); finally, any valuation subring of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, containing the chart algebra and centred at $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the members of `ends`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element $b \in B_t$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ that meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and for which no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$. The hypothesis `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ that is not the $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-translate of $y$ under any level automorphism, an element $b \in B_t$ lying in no valuation subring of $K_\ell$ which contains the chart algebra and is centred at any translate of $y''$. The hypothesis `hn` identifies $n$ with `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the width character of $s$ (at $q = 2$, $12$ or $1$ according as the $j$-value of $s$ vanishes or not, divided by the ramification index of $j$ at $s$).
--
--   **The descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$ generated by all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose members are the elements lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there exists $b \in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$, such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the following two properties. First, for $x \in k_0$ the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $V$ if and only if $x$ lies in $A$. Second, for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ has non-negative order, whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, and for which `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$: this element lies in $K_0$, it lies in $V$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s'.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between it and the image of $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   This is the separation step for the supersingular points on the quotient curve: it produces, for each supersingular place $s'$ other than the distinguished one, a $G$-invariant element of the rigid chart algebra $B_0 = B_t^G$ which has a pole at every valuation ring of the fixed field $K_0$ centred over $s'$, so that the chart built from $s$ sees no other supersingular point. It is stated in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame at $q = 2$, where the level group is $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}(q,M') \cap \ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times)$, and is used by the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at $2$ with its supersingular fibre.
